  "familyDescriptions": {
    "macropodidae": "Kangaroos and wallabies - Australia and New Guinea's hopping marsupials, propelled by powerful hind legs and a thick tail used for balance and, at rest, as a fifth limb.",
    "vombatidae": "Wombats - burrowing Australian marsupials with backward-facing pouches (so digging doesn't bury their joeys) and cube-shaped droppings, unique among mammals."
  }
